          "code": "SUMMARIZE_WORK_ORDER_SHORTAGES",
          "id": "1767899549598",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767899549600_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use  `Shortage` Array to identify shortage material requirements.\n  -  Value : {{$context.$variables.WorkOrderItemShortageDetails}} \n\n- If `Shortage` array is null or empty, return below no data found message:  \n  - `No Work Order material shortages found for the time period`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\n- If data found:\n - Generate one concise, newspaper-style headline (≤ 30 words) highlighting the most critical shortage.\n - Do not list multiple bullets. Do not explain. Do not include internal identifier in display."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1770021084670",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770021084673_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### App/Agent Purpose\n\nThis workflow agent helps identify and resolve material shortages that can prevent maintenance work orders from progressing. It analyzes current shortages on the provided work order, reviews material availability, recommends substitutes or transfers when possible, and enables timely action to address parts needs and reduce maintenance delays.\n\n---\n\n### Maintenance Management Context\n\nMaintenance operations rely on work orders created for assets needing preventive or corrective work. Each work order may involve multiple operations, each with specific resource and material requirements. Estimated costs are based on planned requirements; actual costs reflect executed transactions. This process operates within an organization context, where ensuring material readiness and continuity is essential for minimizing downtime.\n\n#### Key Maintenance Terms  \n- **Work Order:** (e.g., WO, work order number, wo#) — Schedule of required maintenance for an asset, including all associated operations, materials, and resources.\n- **Asset:** (e.g., Asset Number, assetnum, asset#) — The equipment or item being maintained.\n- **Operation:** (operation, OP, op, step, steps) — A distinct task or phase within a work order potentially requiring specific materials.\n- **Organization:** (Organization Code, Org, etc.) — The entity or facility managing the maintenance process.\n\n---\n\n### Data Provided\n\n- **Work Order Shortage Data:**  \n  `{{$context.$variables.WorkOrderItemShortageDetails}}` — Material shortages for the current work order.\n- **Chat History:**  \n  `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n### Task\n\n- Answer the user's query from:  \n  `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` using only the data and context above.\n- Do **not** infer or fabricate information.\n\n---\n\n### Response Rules\n\n- When provided work order `{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}` is present, focus only on shortages for this work order\n  If the user asks about another work order, clearly state this app only works for the specific work order in context.\n- Recommendation summary can be formed using below logic:\n   - If `SubstituteItem` is available: recommend “Substitute Item”\n   - If `OrgsWithStock` > 0: recommend “Request Transfer” \n   - If no Substitute Item and no Orgs With Stock: recommend “Requisition Part”\n   - If `Shortage` is 0: there is no shortage\n- Use only readable names, codes, and descriptions in your response. Do **not** include any internal IDs or technical identifiers.\n- Provide a concise summary or table listing material shortages, their quantities, and recommended actions (such as use of substitute, transfer request, or requisition).\n- If there are no material shortages for the provided work order and User Query, state this explicitly.\n- Do not mention data source or dataset names.\n- Only answer what the user asks in inputMessage; do not suggest other actions or next steps.\n- Do not fabricate or infer missing inputs.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Shortages for Work Order"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_SHORTAGES_FOR_WORK_ORDER",
          "id": "1767890498815",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767890498817_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use the `Shortage` array (`{{$context.$variables.WorkOrderItemShortageDetails}}`) to identify work order material shortages.\n\n- If the `Shortage` array is null or empty:\n  - Return a table with a single column `Information` and one row:  \n    `No Work Order material shortages found for the time period`\n  - Do not ask for clarification or request user input. Only display the specified message.\n\n- If data is present:\n  - Display the results as a `multiRecordWidget` table with the following columns:\n    - Op Seq\n    - Material Seq (`MaterialSequenceNumber`)\n    - Item Number\n    - Item Description\n    - Required Date (date only, without time)\n    - UOM\n    - Required\n    - Open\n    - Shortage\n    - Lead Time\n    - Substitute Item\n    - Orgs With Stock\n    - Recommendation\n     - Recommendation rules:\n      - If Shortage is 0: do not display any recommendation.\n      - If SubstituteItem is available: show \"Substitute Item\" as a badge with warning priority.\n      - Else if OrgsWithStock > 0: show \"Request Transfer\" as a badge with medium priority.\n      - Else: show \"Requisition Part\" as a badge with medium priority.\n  - Generate actionable Insight as per below rules:\n    - Show an Actionable Insight only when SubstituteItem is available.\n    - For rows where SubstituteItem is available, populate the Action column with:\n      - text: Update Substitute\n      - command: ora.Invoke(UpdateSubstitute,{ActionCode: UpdateSubstitute, WorkOrderId, WoOperationId, WoOperationMaterialId, SubstituteItem})\n    - For rows where SubstituteItem is not available, leave the Action column empty.\n\n- Return only the table.\n- Set the overall `title` as `Material Shortages  —  {{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}} `\n- Do not include any internal identifiers (ID) or extra commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Take Shortage Action",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawInput =\n  $context?.$app?.$OraAction ??\n  $context?.$triggers?.REST?.$input?.OraAction ??\n  null;\n\nlet ActionCode = null,\n    WorkOrderId = null,\n    WoOperationId = null,\n    WoOperationMaterialId = null,\n    SubstituteItem = null;\n\nif (rawInput != null) {\n  try {\n    const parsed =\n      typeof rawInput === 'object' ? rawInput : JSON.parse(String(rawInput));\n\n    ActionCode = parsed?.ActionCode ?? null;\n    WorkOrderId = parsed?.WorkOrderId ?? null;\n    WoOperationId = parsed?.WoOperationId ?? null;\n    WoOperationMaterialId = parsed?.WoOperationMaterialId ?? null;\n    SubstituteItem = parsed?.SubstituteItem ?? null;\n  } catch {\n    // Fallback: comma-separated values\n    const parts = String(rawInput).split(',').map(s => s.trim());\n    [ActionCode, WorkOrderId, WoOperationId, WoOperationMaterialId, SubstituteItem] =\n      [parts[0] ?? null, parts[1] ?? null, parts[2] ?? null, parts[3] ?? null, parts[4] ?? null];\n  }\n}\n\nconst retValue = {\n  ActionCode,\n  WorkOrderId,\n  WoOperationId,\n  WoOperationMaterialId,\n  SubstituteItem,\n};\n\nreturn retValue;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768253008150"
          },
          "code": "TAKE_SHORTAGE_ACTION",
          "id": "1768252755373",
