        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Work Order Data from User Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771222089644"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_WORK_ORDER_DATA_FROM_USER_QUERY",
          "id": "1771221801724",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771221801726_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract data from the user query: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` and build a valid REST `q` parameter (`pQparam`) for searching work orders, which can be directly used in a REST call.\n\n**Build pQparam:**\n- Extract relevant parameter values and construct `pQparam` using valid Oracle REST Query Language (RQL) syntax.\n- For BETWEEN clauses, always use parentheses.  \n  Example: `(PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-02-09' AND '2025-02-10')`\n- The current date `CurrentDate` value is `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`. \n- If `OrganizationId` is available (`{{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}`), MUST always include the below clause:  \n  `OrganizationId = {{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}`\n- If `WorkOrderNumber` is available (` {{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}`), MUST include the clause:  \n  `WorkOrderNumber = '{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}'`\n\n**Important Constraints:**\n- For any user query, do **not** include or infer shortage, inventory, substitute, transfer, requisition, or fulfillment fields or logic in the `q` param—use only fields that are directly searchable on the WorkOrder REST API.\n  - Business logic for material shortage or resolution (such as transfer, substitute, requisition) will be applied later and never in this q parameter.\n- **Do not** append any additional clause like:  \n  - `onHandQuantity < RequiredQuantity`\n  - `RequirementQuantity > IssuedQuantity`\n  - `ShortageQuantity > 0`\n  - `TransferLocationId`\n  - `IsPurchasable`\n  - `SupplierId`\n  - `SubstituteItemNumber`\n  - or any similar field not directly supported in work order searches.\n\n**Examples:**  \n1) Get item and material shortage (Both `OrganizationId` and `WorkOrderNumber` are available))\n`pQparam` = \"OrganizationId = 123456 AND WorkOrderNumber ='JKJWO1'\"\n2) Get all information for work order that starts with JKJ WO 001 and  having unfulfilled item requirement for m-assy-srl-p (Only `OrganizationId` available)\n`pQparam` = \"OrganizationId = 123456 AND WorkOrderNumber like UPPER('JKJ WO 001%25')  AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationMaterial.InventoryItemNumber = 'm-assy-srl-p'\"\n3) Get information on item requirement for m-srl-lot  in last 1 month (Only `WorkOrderNumber` available)\n`pQparam` = \"WorkOrderNumber ='JKJWO1' AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationMaterial.InventoryItemNumber = 'm-srl-lot' AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-02-09' AND '2025-03-11')\"\n4) Example for a complex pQparam\n`pQparam` = \"UPPER(WorkOrderNumber) like UPPER('aBc%25') AND (AssetNumber = 'Asset_001' OR AssetNumber = 'Asset_003' ) AND WorkOrderDescription like 'ABC Wo%25' AND WorkOrderTypeCode != 'CORRECTIVE' AND WorkOrderSubTypeCode=UPPER('ora_planned') AND WorkOrderStatusCode IN ('ORA_RELEASED','ORA_UNRELEASED') AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-03-07' and '2026-06-24' ) AND WorkOrderOperation.OperationSequenceNumber = 10 AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationResource.ResourceCode IS NULL AND attachments.DocumentPreviewURL IS NOT NULL AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationMaterial.InventoryItemNumber = 'm-assy-srl-p'\"\n\nReturn only the constructed `pQparam` string. \nNever return an error or explanation—always return a valid query string, defaulting WorkOrderNumber clause if the user input is missing or unclear."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"pQparam\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
